The height slicer's call-site change for the SPARSE height planes.
=================================================================

    git apply docs/overlay-sparse-planes.patch

WHY THIS IS A PATCH AND NOT A COMMIT
------------------------------------
src/overlay.cpp is owned by another workstream in this release, so the branch that
made the height planes sparse (mapdata.cpp/.hpp, review item C.14) could not edit it.
Everything else is done and builds; this is the last four hunks.

WHAT CHANGED UNDER IT
---------------------
The planes were eight dense `width * height` uint16 arrays - 343 MB for chapter 1, of
which 74 % was the code 0 ("no surface here"). They are now 128-px blocks with an
index, and only the non-empty blocks are allocated: 86 MB for chapter 1, 47..74 MB for
chapters 2-5. An absent block reads as code 0, so no ANSWER changes.

What does change is that a row of the picture crosses several blocks, so there is no
row pointer to hand out. `hm.plane[k].data()` + `plane + sy * hm.width` becomes
`hm.gather_row(k, sy, col_x, w, scratch)`, which fills one destination row of codes -
the same `w` reads per plane per row the dense version did, plus one index lookup per
128 columns - and returns false when the row has no surface at all, which lets the
slicer skip most rows of the deeper planes outright.

THE FOUR HUNKS
--------------
  1. `SliceScratch` gains `std::vector<std::uint16_t> gather` (and clears it).
  2. It is sized next to `col_x`, which is already per-slicer.
  3. `slice_region()`'s plane loop: `plane_empty(k)` instead of `plane[k].empty()`,
     `gather_row()` instead of the row pointer, and the inner loop reads `gathered[col]`
     instead of `src[col_x[col]]` - so the `sx < 0` test disappears, because a column
     outside the asset gathers as code 0.
  4. The slicer self-test's "find a lit pixel" scan becomes `hm.first_lit(0, ...)`,
     which the block index answers directly instead of striding over 43 MB.

UNTIL IT IS APPLIED, the deprecated (and empty) `plane[]` shim in mapdata.hpp makes
the slicer skip every surface: the build produces three C4996 warnings naming the
call sites, and mapdata.cpp logs "NOTE the height slicer in overlay.cpp still reads
the dense `plane[]` member" at every chapter load. Delete the shim once this lands.

Verified: with this patch applied the DLL compiles clean (no C4996) against
mapdata.hpp as committed.

